w: 1.~O sac- red Head, now wound- ed, with grief and shame * weighed down, 
w: 2.~What Thou, my Lord, hast suf- fered, was all for sin- * ners' gain; 
w: 3.~Men mock and taunt and jeer Thee, Thou no- ble coun- * ten- ance, 
w: 4.~Now from Thy cheeks has van- ished their co- lor once * so fair; 
w: 5.~My bur- den in Thy Pas- sion, Lord, Thou hast borne * for me, 
w: 6.~What lang- uage shall I bor- row to thank Thee, dear- _ est friend,
w: 7.~My Shep- herd, now re- ceive me; my Guard- ian, own _ me Thine.
w: 8.~Here I will stand be- side Thee, from Thee I will _ not part;
w: 9.~The joy can never be spo- ken, a- bove all joys _ be- side,
w: 10.~My Sa- vior, be Thou near me when death is at _ my door;
w: 11.~Be Thou my con- so- la- tion, my shield when I _ must die;
