w: O sac- * red Head, what glo- ry, what bliss till now was Thine! 
w: Lo, here * I fall, my Sa- vior! 'Tis I de- serve Thy place; 
w: How art * thou pale with an- guish, with sore a- buse and scorn! 
w: Grim death, * with cru- el ri- gor, hath robbed Thee of Thy life; 
w: I cast * me down be- fore Thee, wrath were my right- ful lot; 
w: O make _ me Thine for- ev- er, and should I faint- ing be,
w: Thy lips _ have of- ten fed me with words of truth and love;
w: When soul _ and bo- dy lan- guish in death's cold, cru- el grasp,
w: O Lord _ of Life, de- si- ring Thy glo- ry now to see,
w: When soul _ and bo- dy lan- guish, oh, leave me not a- lone,
w: Mine eyes _ shall then be- hold Thee, up- on Thy cross shall dwell,
